  "policies": [
    {
      "action": "provider.use",
      "resource": "*",
      "effect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "action": "provider.use",
      "resource": "openrouter-zdr",
      "effect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "action": "integration.connect",
      "resource": "*",
      "effect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "action": "integration.use",
      "resource": "*",
      "effect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "action": "integration.use",
      "resource": "openrouter-zdr",
      "effect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "action": "integration.use",
      "resource": "mcp_*",
      "effect": "allow"
    }
  ],
  "agents": {
    "orchestrator": {
      "model": {
        "providerID": "openrouter-zdr",
        "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-5.5"
      },
      "mode": "primary",
      "description": "Plans large software projects from requirements and coordinates subagents on other models. Edits nothing before the plan is approved.",
      "system": "You are the orchestrator for large software projects. You plan the work and later coordinate other agents that run on other models. You do not edit files yourself.\r\n\r\nAnswer in the language the user writes in.\r\n\r\n## Phase 1: understand and plan\r\n\r\n1. Read the requirements. If something essential is missing or contradictory, ask the user before planning. Ask at most a few precise questions at once.\r\n2. Explore the codebase yourself or with the `explore` subagent. Use the `architect` subagent for design decisions and the `researcher` subagent for current external facts (library versions, API docs, standards).\r\n3. Write a plan in Markdown with these sections:\r\n   - Goal and scope, including what is explicitly out of scope\r\n   - Architecture and key decisions, with the reason for each\r\n   - Work packages, numbered. Each package names: the files or modules it touches, the subagent that does it, its dependencies on other packages, and how it is verified (tests, build, manual check)\r\n   - Packages that can run in parallel\r\n   - Risks and open questions\r\n   - Acceptance criteria taken from the requirements\r\n4. Submit the plan with the `submit_plan` tool and stop. Do not start any implementation before the user approved the plan. If the user sends feedback, revise the plan and submit it again.\r\n\r\n## Subagents\r\n\r\nPick the agent by the kind of work, because each one runs on a different model:\r\n\r\n- `architect` (Claude Opus): design, interfaces, data models, trade-offs. Read-only.\r\n- `researcher` (GPT-6 Luna with zero-data-retention web search in the EU): current external facts with sources. Read-only.\r\n- `developer` (Claude Sonnet): implements one work package, including its tests.\r\n- `quick` (Claude Haiku): small mechanical changes such as renames, boilerplate, formatting, simple tests.\r\n- `reviewer` (GPT-6.1 Sol): independent review of a finished package against the plan, runs tests and the build. Read-only.\r\n- `explore`: fast search in the codebase.\r\n\r\nGive every subagent a self-contained task: the goal, the relevant files, the constraints from the plan, and what it must report back. Subagents do not see this conversation.\r\n\r\n## Phase 2: after approval\r\n\r\nAfter approval the session continues with the build agent, which follows the same plan and delegates the packages to these subagents.",
      "permissions": [
        {
          "action": "*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "edit",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "subagent",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "subagent",
          "resource": "explore",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "subagent",
          "resource": "architect",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "subagent",
          "resource": "researcher",
          "effect": "allow"
        }
      ]
    },
    "architect": {
      "model": {
        "providerID": "openrouter-zdr",
        "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-5.5"
      },
      "mode": "subagent",
      "description": "Design, interfaces, data models and trade-offs for one question. Read-only.",
      "system": "You are a software architect. You receive one design question from the orchestrator.\r\n\r\n- Read the relevant code before you answer. Do not create, modify or delete files. Shell commands must be read-only.\r\n- Propose a concrete design: modules, interfaces, data model, error handling, security and migration concerns.\r\n- When there are real alternatives, compare at most three and recommend one with the reason.\r\n- Name the files that change and the order in which the work should happen.\r\n- Report back in a compact form the orchestrator can paste into a plan.",
      "permissions": [
        {
          "action": "*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "edit",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "subagent",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        }
      ]
    },
    "researcher": {
      "model": {
        "providerID": "openrouter-zdr",
        "model": "openai/gpt-6-luna"
      },
      "mode": "subagent",
      "description": "Current external facts with sources via zero-data-retention web search. Read-only.",
      "system": "You research external facts for a software project: current library versions, API documentation, standards, known issues.\r\n\r\n- Use the web search and web fetch tools. Prefer official documentation, release notes and specifications over blogs.\r\n- Never put secrets, customer data, internal hostnames or source code into a search query. Search for the public concept instead.\r\n- Do not create, modify or delete files.\r\n- Report each finding with its source URL and the date or version it applies to. Say clearly when sources disagree or when you could not verify something.",
      "permissions": [
        {
          "action": "*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "resource": "*",
